{title: 458 - More Love to Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #458 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 458}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]More [C]love [G]to Thee, [D]O [G]Christ,
[G]More [D]love [A7]to [D]Thee!
[G]Hear [C]Thou [G]the prayer [D]I [G]make
[D7]On [G]bend[D7]ed [G]knee.
[C]This is my ear[G]nest plea,
[D7]More love, O Christ, [G]to Thee;
[C]More love to [G]Thee,
[Am]More [G]love [D]to [G]Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Once [C]earthly joy [G]I craved, [D]sought peace [G]and rest;
[G]now thee [D]alone I [A7]seek, give [D]what is best.
[G]This all [C]my prayer [G]shall be: More [D]love, O [G]Christ, to thee;
[D7]more love [G]to thee, [D7]more love [G]to thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Let [C]sorrow do [G]its work, [D]come grief [G]and pain;
[G]sweet [D]are thy [A7]messengers, sweet [D]their refrain,
[G]when they [C]can sing [G]with me: More [D]love, O [G]Christ, to thee;
[D7]more love [G]to thee, [D7]more love [G]to thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Then [C]shall my [G]latest [D]breath whisper [G]thy praise;
[G]this be [D]the parting [A7]cry my [D]heart shall raise;
[G]this still [C]its prayer [G]shall be: More [D]love, O [G]Christ, to thee;
[D7]more love [G]to thee, [D7]more love [G]to thee!
{end_of_verse}
